## Phase 1 — Domain and ingestion

### F1. Domain core

**Depends on:** F0.

**Files:** `src/Domain/src/Dispute/`

**What to do:**

An EventSauce `DisputeAggregate` plus value objects and a
`DisputeAggregateRepositoryInterface` (`retrieve` / `persist`, mirroring
`PaymentIntentAggregateRepositoryInterface`). No gateway code whatsoever.

```
DisputeAggregate (aggregate root)
  DisputeId              — UuidValueObject subclass, ours, not the provider's
  PaymentIntentId
  GatewayDisputeRef      — string; may contain / and + (Nuvei)
  DisputeStage           — INQUIRY | CHARGEBACK | PRE_ARBITRATION | ARBITRATION
  DisputeStatus          — NEEDS_RESPONSE | UNDER_REVIEW | WON | LOST | ACCEPTED | EXPIRED | CLOSED
  SubmissionState        — NONE | DRAFT | UPLOAD_PENDING | SUBMITTED | CONFIRMED   (second axis, see below)
  DisputeReason          — { CardBrand, string rawCode, ReasonCategory }
  Money disputedAmount
  Money disputeFee
  DeadlineAt  { \DateTimeImmutable at, bool isAuthoritative }
  DisputeEvent[]         — stage history
```

No `GatewayAccountId` field — §0.4.

**`SubmissionState` is a separate axis on purpose.** The provider's view of the case and our view of
our own submission attempt move independently: Nuvei sits in "file uploaded, callback not yet
received" while the provider still reports `NEEDS_RESPONSE`, and ConnexPay has an operator who
claims to have submitted while `HasResponse` is still `false`. Folding these into `DisputeStatus`
means F9 and A3 come back to rewrite F1's invariants. Two axes, each with its own transitions.

**Events:** `DisputeOpened`, `DisputeStageChanged`, `DisputeStatusChanged`, `DisputeDeadlineChanged`,
`EvidenceAttached`, `EvidenceSubmitted`, `EvidenceUploadConfirmed`, `DisputeResolved`,
`DisputeAccepted`.

**Invariants that must be covered by tests:**

- The `LOST → WON` transition **is allowed**. Stripe labels these as late wins; an issuer may credit
  outside the normal cycle. Test: aggregate in `LOST`, apply `DisputeResolved(WON)` — no exception.
- `ACCEPTED` is terminal; no transition back out.
- `EXPIRED` is only reachable from a provider signal or from an explicit expiry command issued by
  the application's clock. The aggregate has no timer of its own.
- `DisputeReason` stores the raw code **and** the `CardBrand` **and** the category. Mapping raw code
  to category lives in a separate table-driven `ReasonCodeMapper` under `ValueObject/`. Visa `13.1`,
  Mastercard `4853` and Amex `C08` do not collapse into one enum: evidence requirements differ, and
  the hint logic hangs off the (brand, raw code) pair.
- `DeadlineAt.isAuthoritative = false` when the date was computed by us rather than supplied by the
  provider. This affects both the UI and escalation.
- Idempotency: re-applying the same external signal produces no new domain event. The key is
  `(GatewayId, GatewayDisputeRef, providerEventKey)`, where `GatewayId` comes from the message
  header and `providerEventKey` is defined **per provider**:
  - Stripe — the webhook `event.id` (already `ParsedEvent::$externalId`).
  - Nuvei — `DisputeEventId`.
  - ConnexPay — **there is no event id.** The key is a stable hash of the case's normalised state
    snapshot, computed by the adapter in F5. Fix the hashing contract here (which fields, what
    normalisation) so F5 cannot drift from it.

**Done when:** aggregate unit tests are green under `--testsuite=Domain`, including every invariant
above and at least one test per `providerEventKey` shape. Not a single line of gateway code.

